# DINGLECRAFT Licence (source-available, no redistribution)

Copyright (c) 2026 Dan Dingle. All rights reserved, except as set out below.

DINGLECRAFT is source-available, not open source. You may read the code, play the game and tinker with it. You may not
hand it out.

## 1. What you may do

1. **Play it.** Download, run and play DINGLECRAFT for free.
2. **Tinker with it.** Read the code, change it and run your changed version, for your own personal, non-commercial use.
3. **Fork it on GitHub and contribute.** You may fork this repository on GitHub, as GitHub's Terms of Service allow, and
   send pull requests.
4. **Make videos and screenshots.** You may record, stream and publish videos, screenshots and other media of yourself
   playing, and you may monetise them. A credit or a link back is appreciated but not required.

## 2. What you may not do without written permission from Dan Dingle

1. **Redistribute it.** No re-uploading, mirroring, rehosting, repackaging, publishing to app stores or game sites, or
   sharing copies of the game, its source code or its assets anywhere except through GitHub's fork feature. This applies
   to modified and unmodified versions alike.
2. **Sell it or use it commercially.** No selling, sublicensing or bundling of the game, the code or the assets, and no
   other commercial use. Gameplay videos are the exception set out in section 1.
3. **Use the assets elsewhere.** The art, models, textures, sounds and music may not be used in other projects.
4. **Remove this notice.** This licence and the copyright notice must stay with any copy you make under it.

## 3. Third-party components

Components listed in [THIRD_PARTY.md](THIRD_PARTY.md) remain under their own licences. Nothing in this licence limits
the rights those licences give you.

